      "sequence_position": 5,
      "problem": "For two independent random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\text{Var}[X]=12$ and $\\text{Var}[Y]=5.$ Find $\\text{Var}[X-Y].$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are independent random variables, then \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X\\pm Y]=\\text{Var}[X]+\\text{Var}[Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X-Y]=12+5=17.\n$$",
